-- library.nlir: shared concepts across rules. Binds $nodes: a list of {rule, node, kind, text} — the nodes of the
-- rules' models, usually one kind at a time. Groups nodes from DIFFERENT rules that name the same consideration into a
-- shared concept with a short name and a one-sentence definition in the policy's own terms; a node no other rule
-- shares stays out. Compact output (members as "rule|node") so a whole policy fits in one reply.
$json%($parse%(=>("Below are nodes of small models of several policy rules: each names the action being judged, a condition that must hold for a violation, a permitted exception, or a fact a verdict turns on. Group nodes from DIFFERENT rules that name the same consideration — the same kind of evidence, exception, threshold, actor or fact, even if worded differently or applied to a different action — into shared concepts. Only group nodes whose meaning genuinely coincides; do not group by topic alone. Leave out any node that no other rule shares.\n\nReply with compact JSON only: {\"concepts\": [{\"name\": \"<short noun phrase>\", \"def\": \"<one sentence, at most 15 words>\", \"m\": [\"<rule>|<node>\", ...]}]}\n\nNODES:\n" ++ $json%$nodes)))
